{
  "description": "Integrate Microsoft Fabric Lakehouse SQL Analytics Endpoint as a read-only SQL\nquery platform for benchmarking pre-loaded Delta Lake tables.\n\n**Critical Architectural Constraint**:\nThe Lakehouse SQL Analytics Endpoint is READ-ONLY. This is a fundamental Fabric\ndesign choice, not a BenchBox limitation:\n- NO DDL: Cannot CREATE TABLE, DROP TABLE, ALTER TABLE\n- NO DML: Cannot INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE, MERGE\n- QUERY ONLY: SELECT statements only\n\n**Data Loading Requirement**:\nData MUST be loaded via Microsoft Fabric Spark Notebooks (see related TODO:\nfabric-spark-notebooks-platform.yaml). The workflow is:\n1. Use Fabric Spark to load data into Lakehouse Delta tables\n2. Use this adapter to benchmark query performance via SQL endpoint\n\nThis is a valid benchmarking pattern for:\n- Measuring query-only performance (common for BI/reporting workloads)\n- Comparing Lakehouse SQL endpoint vs Fabric Warehouse performance\n- Testing Delta Lake query optimization (V-Order, Z-Order effects)\n\nThe adapter will explicitly validate the read-only constraint and fail fast\nwith helpful error messages if users attempt write operations.\n\nTechnical characteristics:\n- T-SQL dialect (subset compatible with Synapse/SQL Server)\n- TDS protocol via pyodbc (same as Fabric Warehouse)\n- Entra ID authentication only\n- Automatic Delta Lake to SQL type mapping\n- OneLake-backed storage (transparent to queries)\n\nReference: fabric_warehouse.py:14-30 documents this limitation explicitly:\n\"Lakehouse: SQL Analytics Endpoint is READ-ONLY (not supported)\"\nThis adapter provides READ-ONLY support as a deliberate feature.",
